 When the composition provides `ctx.sessionProjections`, token-meter registers four projection units. `tokenUsage` carries the complete durable log's `uncachedInputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens`, and `cacheWriteTokens`. A final assistant-message sample replaces streaming usage from the same attempt; `llm/retry-started` ends that replacement scope, so a retry in the same step contributes another billed attempt. `modelCost` commits only complete normal-Turn accounting and publishes per-currency totals plus reported/estimated/virtual buckets without currency conversion; its coverage counts accounted and unaccounted model Turns so a known subtotal is never mistaken for complete Session spend. `contextPressure` carries optional `pressureTokens` (the newest provider-reported prompt size), optional `projectedTokens` (what the next request's prompt would cost), and optional `contextWindow` from the newest `request/context` record. `contextBreakdown` carries heuristic `systemTokens`, `toolsTokens`, and `messageTokens` — the context's composition, not its provider-billed size. Unloading the plugin removes all four keys.
 
-`deriveTurnCost(events)` uses the durable attempt/retry/step boundaries to aggregate every accounted attempt exactly once. Missing accounting, contradictory top-level and embedded values, incomplete lifecycle, malformed nanos, or an unsafe sum omits the complete Turn result; details retain route, source, tariff provenance, and component nanos when every grouped call reported that component while compact totals remain grouped by currency.
+`deriveTurnCost(events)` uses the durable attempt/retry/step boundaries to aggregate every accounted attempt exactly once. Missing accounting, contradictory top-level and embedded values, incomplete lifecycle, malformed nanos, or an unsafe sum omits the complete Turn result; a final `turn`-scoped Assistant message instead replaces prior call costs and covers earlier missing Tool-attempt accounting, but any later settlement, retry, or Step invalidates it; details retain route, source, tariff provenance, and component nanos when every grouped call reported that component while compact totals remain grouped by currency.
 
 `contextBreakdown` classifies the last nonempty surviving `system/message` in surface order as `systemTokens`; empty dormant nodes contribute nothing, and no nonempty system means zero. `messageTokens` includes every other visible node, including superseded prompts. Their sum always equals `measure().nodes[].heuristicTokens`, including after unmetered replacements, compaction, and per-node prompt clearing. `toolsTokens` follows the latest `request/header`. All three use the fixed heuristic, not route image pricing or file-handle projection; they are approximate composition, not billing or `projectedTokens`.
 
